Apollo @PROJECT_VERSION@
A cross-platform wavetable synthesizer by ProdByRnV

WHAT IS IN THIS PACKAGE

  VST3/Apollo.vst3        the plugin, for a DAW
  Standalone/             Apollo as an application, needing no DAW
  INSTALL.txt             this file

  Nothing here is an installer. Apollo is a folder you copy, and removing it
  is deleting that folder again.


INSTALLING THE PLUGIN

  Copy the whole "Apollo.vst3" folder — not the file inside it — into the
  place your system keeps VST3 plugins:

  Windows     C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3
              or, without administrator rights:
              %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Common\VST3

  macOS       /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3
              or, for one user only:
              ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3

  Linux       /usr/lib/vst3
              or, for one user only:
              ~/.vst3

  Then rescan your plugins in your DAW. Most hosts do this on startup; some
  have a button for it.


RUNNING THE STANDALONE

  Open the application in the Standalone folder. It has its own audio and
  MIDI settings, and does not need a DAW or the plugin to be installed.


WHAT APOLLO NEEDS

  A 64-bit system. On Windows, Windows 10 or later.

  On Windows, the Microsoft Edge WebView2 runtime, which draws Apollo's
  interface. Windows 11 has it already; Windows 10 usually does, because it
  arrives with Microsoft Edge. If Apollo's window opens without an interface,
  install "Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime" from Microsoft and reopen it.

  You do NOT need the Visual C++ Redistributable. Apollo carries what it
  needs of that runtime inside itself.

  Nothing else. Apollo does not require an internet connection, and it does
  not phone anywhere while you use it.


WHERE APOLLO KEEPS YOUR THINGS

  Presets you save go to your own settings folder, not into this folder, so
  replacing Apollo with a newer version never touches them:

  Windows     %APPDATA%\Apollo\Presets
  macOS       ~/Library/Apollo/Presets
  Linux       ~/.config/Apollo/Presets

  The sounds Apollo ships with are built into the plugin itself. They cannot
  be lost, and they are there the first time you open it.


VERSION

  Apollo @PROJECT_VERSION@, built for @APOLLO_PACKAGE_SYSTEM@ on @APOLLO_PACKAGE_ARCH@.
